Gäld is installed under /srv/www/gaeld. The document root is
/srv/www/gaeld/public. Configuration is /etc/gaeld/gaeld.env
(symlinked to /srv/www/gaeld/.env).

1. Create the database (PostgreSQL) and a Redis instance:

   su - postgres -c "createuser -P gaeld"
   su - postgres -c "createdb -O gaeld gaeld"
   systemctl enable --now postgresql redis

2. Edit /etc/gaeld/gaeld.env. Set DB_PASSWORD, APP_URL, and the
   hostname used in WEBAUTHN_ID. APP_URL must be the URL users open
   in the browser, including https:// when TLS is terminated in front.

3. Enable a web server integration and the queue:

   # nginx (packaged site: /etc/nginx/sites-available/gaeld.conf)
   ln -s ../sites-available/gaeld.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/gaeld.conf
   systemctl enable --now php-fpm@gaeld nginx

   # or Apache: the snippet in
   # /etc/httpd/conf/webapps.d/gaeld.conf expects a vhost whose
   # DocumentRoot is /srv/www/gaeld/public and mod_proxy_fcgi.
   systemctl enable --now php-fpm@gaeld httpd

   systemctl enable --now gaeld-horizon.service gaeld-scheduler.timer

4. Install the application (creates the admin user and the Swiss
   chart of accounts):

   gaeld gaeld:install

   On later package upgrades the rpm runs gaeld:update when APP_KEY
   is already set.

Receipt OCR needs tesseract and the deu, fra, and eng language packs.
Search stays on the database driver. Meilisearch is optional; see
SCOUT_DRIVER in the environment file.
